[profiles.guide]
notes = '''This is the gyro variant: tilting the controller moves the cursor, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The campaign map and battles play very differently, so this setup has a scheme for each. Hold {select} to pick Campaign map or Battle with {lb} {rb} and {confirm}: switch when a battle starts and when it ends. The scheme in use shows at the top of the screen.
Both: the right stick {rs} moves the cursor, {rt} selects (left click, hold to drag a box) and {lt} moves and attacks (right click; drag it to set the line's width). The left stick {ls} moves the camera (WASD), {up} {down} zoom and {left} {right} rotate it. {east} closes a panel or deselects, {start} is the game menu; double tap {start} to quick save, hold it to quick load.
Campaign map: {south} is a left click as well. Hold {north} to end the turn. {select} lists the end turn, technology, saving and loading.
Battle: {south} halts, {west} toggles running, {north} toggles fire at will, {l3} groups the selected units and {r3} pauses. Hold {lb} for the control groups and aim the right stick {rs}; hold {lb} and {rb} together to set one instead. {rb} is Ctrl: hold it to add units to the selection. {select} lists pause, select all and the other orders.
Empire has no tactical map, so {r3} pauses instead. Formations, ammunition and ships' sail speeds are on the unit card: click them. Sea battles use the Battle scheme too.
The keys are the defaults as best known, not checked on an install. The Linux executable name (Empire, Feral's port) is a guess; Empire.exe comes from Discord's game list, and the other ids the wiki lists for the game are DLC, so only 10500 is kept. If a key does nothing, look in Options, Controls and set it to the key in this setup.'''

